{"id":"b56049ecb5df84b2","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class.md","title":"ZFC Forcing Axiom For Class","display":"df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class — ZFC Forcing Axiom For Class","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class","aliases":["58-df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class"],"display":"df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class — ZFC Forcing Axiom For Class","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-dense.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-pair.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-forcing-axiom-for-class — ZFC Forcing Axiom For Class"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"681e6314e26cdd0b\" href=\"?note=681e6314e26cdd0b\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-dense.md\">../batch10/58-df-dense.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" href=\"?note=bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset.md\">../batch07/58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f16f4ca5b9c48bbe\" href=\"?note=f16f4ca5b9c48bbe\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-pair.md\">../batch12/58-df-pair.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma,\\lambda\\in V\">\\(\\Gamma,\\lambda\\in V\\)</span> (set-coded family of ordered pairs <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle P,\\leq_P\\rangle\">\\(\\langle P,\\leq_P\\rangle\\)</span> and cardinal bound)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingAxiomForClass}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingAxiomForClass}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Dense}(D,P,\\leq_P)\">\\(\\operatorname{Dense}(D,P,\\leq_P)\\)</span> (dense subset predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"681e6314e26cdd0b\" href=\"?note=681e6314e26cdd0b\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-dense.md\">../batch10/58-df-dense.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FilterOnPoset}(G,P,\\leq_P)\">\\(\\operatorname{FilterOnPoset}(G,P,\\leq_P)\\)</span> (filter on a poset, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" href=\"?note=bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset.md\">../batch07/58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}for\\text{-}class}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingAxiomForClass}_S(\\Gamma,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\n\\forall z\\in\\Gamma\\;\\exists P,\\leq_P\\in V\\;\\Bigl(z=\\langle P,\\leq_P\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathcal D\\subseteq\\mathcal P(P)\\;\\Bigl(\n(|\\mathcal D|\\leq\\lambda\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;\\operatorname{Dense}(D,P,\\leq_P))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists G\\subseteq P\\;\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{FilterOnPoset}(G,P,\\leq_P)\n\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;(G\\cap D\\neq\\varnothing)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}for\\text{-}class}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingAxiomForClass}_S(\\Gamma,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\n\\forall z\\in\\Gamma\\;\\exists P,\\leq_P\\in V\\;\\Bigl(z=\\langle P,\\leq_P\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathcal D\\subseteq\\mathcal P(P)\\;\\Bigl(\n(|\\mathcal D|\\leq\\lambda\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;\\operatorname{Dense}(D,P,\\leq_P))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists G\\subseteq P\\;\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{FilterOnPoset}(G,P,\\leq_P)\n\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;(G\\cap D\\neq\\varnothing)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Each member of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\">\\(\\Gamma\\)</span> explicitly carries both a forcing carrier and its order relation; density and filterhood therefore use their canonical three-place signatures.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-dense.md","status":"resolved","id":"681e6314e26cdd0b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnc